      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and full call trace, exact pre-exploit balances and token metadata, both source repositories, proxy creation, complete upgrade history, EIP-1967 state transitions, implementation runtimes, and historical prices. The exploit transaction directly creates orchestrator 0x33fb722c76d4e9fc0c86bbf10ebdea45a4434a34, which creates asset-list helper 0x92df7b51734d4d8f5de7676ab193ff2138cb4b5c and malicious delegate 0x67da0e9245e2a9da74ac120d8c3caac21b9884da. It calls initialize on proxy 0x30bd8eab29181f790d7e495786d4b96d7afdc518, which delegates selector 0x92413afe to implementation 0xc038933d0b33359f5c87b4b2f92ee0dad11eadc5 and then delegates init() to the attacker-supplied wallet-operations address. That malicious delegate runs in proxy storage context, obtains the beneficiary and 26-token list from the helper, and transfers every nonzero balance to 0x777253f28adc29645152b7b41be5c772a9657777. The subsequent updateWallet call delegates to the same module but finds the balances already zero. Project source commit 35c88f436442077a4925ba148c29f3c3efa52ab5, committed immediately before activation, shows initialize first delegatecalling caller-supplied Merkle and transfer modules, transferring ownership to msg.sender, and setting all supplied delegate addresses; only after those effects does _initialize(storage, 2) check and record version 2. The proxy had not consumed version 2 during the upgrade, so the attacker could execute the whole path. The receipt contains exactly 26 proxy-to-attacker token transfers. Nineteen reliably priced components total $209,196.4623298068 at preceding DefiLlama observations; seven additional exact token quantities are left unpriced. The proxy was directly created by 0x98e4e5c6223bb2cc945a7c2821e30929deff3568 in transaction 0x1a67f80611ad5e5f2a838fb69c0bfd0616482ec903bbda50f3d8c580009658ba, block 249784924 index 7, timestamp 1725399710, and has no code in the preceding block. A complete log query returns 14